***conformance tests***

# replace-in-scenario
The first functionality f1 of a tree has a conformance scenario `greets` whose text is `It prints ` followed by the placeholder of `greeting` and `.`, with code_variables [{name `greeting`, value `hello`}].
- The specifications for f1 hold the conformance scenario {id `greets`, text `It prints hello.`}.
- The code variables are {`greeting`: `hello`}.

# replacement-off
With replacement turned off, the same scenario keeps its placeholder text and the code variables are still {`greeting`: `hello`}.

***acceptance tests***
